OldMailboxMockTest::initialize
├── it should never revert when parameters are valid.
├── when params_ids and params_modules have different lengths
│   └── it should revert.
├── when params_ids is empty
│   └── it should revert.
└── when params_modules is empty
    └── it should revert.


OldMailboxMockTest::addModule
├── it should never revert when the caller has admin role.
├── when the caller does not have admin role
│   └── it should revert.
└── when the module ID already exists
    └── it should revert.


OldMailboxMockTest::_authorizeUpgrade
├── it should never revert when the caller has admin role.
└── when the caller does not have admin role
    └── it should revert.


OldMailboxMockTest::generateRandomNonce
├── it should return a non-zero value.
└── it should return different values on subsequent calls.


OldMailboxMockTest::generateChainId
└── it should return consistent values for the same input.


OldMailboxMockTest::getLastNonce
└── it should return the correct value.


OldMailboxMockTest::getEthereumChainId
└── it should return the correct value.


OldMailboxMockTest::getEclipseChainId
└── it should return the correct value.


OldMailboxMockTest::getModuleAddress
├── when the module ID exists
│   └── it should return the correct address.
└── when the module ID does not exist
    └── it should return the zero address.


OldMailboxMockTest::isReceiveNonceUsed
├── when the nonce has been used
│   └── it should return true.
└── when the nonce has not been used
    └── it should return false.


OldMailboxMockTest::isSendNonceUsed
├── when the nonce has been used
│   └── it should return true.
└── when the nonce has not been used
    └── it should return false.


OldMailboxMockTest::getVersion
└── it should return correct version numbers.

